+# Narrowing the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declared search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian out of scope. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, and its provenance stayed open.
+
+The product owner has asked for the veterinarian directory to be narrowed to one specialty (2026-08-23). Specialty is an attribute the directory already displays beside every name. The [2026-08-08 non-goal ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) set the rule that a request never reopens a row by implication, so the row needs an explicit decision.
+
+The same request reinstates the machine-readable veterinarian list, withdrawn as `REQ-VET-002` on 2026-07-31, as a supported surface.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-9 whole and decline the request.** Rejected: the owner wants the capability, and the row's stated reason covers repeated free-text search, not attribute narrowing.
+2. **Retire NG-9 entirely.** Free-text search for veterinarians would follow. Rejected: owner search already demonstrates paged prefix search over free text once, so a second instance adds surface without teaching.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 keeps free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian out of scope. Narrowing the veterinarian directory to the veterinarians holding one named specialty is in scope, because the directory already publishes that attribute.
+
+The machine-readable veterinarian list is a supported surface again, under the fresh requirement `REQ-VET-003`. `REQ-VET-002` stays withdrawn, and its ID is never reused.
+
+A visible control for choosing a specialty is deferred, not declined. It stays out of the current slice and may arrive as a follow-up request.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation, narrowed rather than confirmed. Every other undecided row remains part of it.
+- The directory publishes one narrowing capability. A request for free-text veterinarian search still needs an explicit owner decision.
+- The machine-readable list carries a requirement, so it is no longer a route pending removal.
+- Deferring the visible control keeps a later request cheap: it adds a way to reach an existing capability, not the capability itself.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD REQ-VET-003](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
