+# Specialty Filtering Runs as an Uncached, Case-Folding Database Query
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+`REQ-VET-003` narrows both veterinarian directory routes to one named specialty. Matching is case-insensitive on the whole name, and both routes must behave alike on H2, MySQL, and PostgreSQL.
+
+Two existing facts shape the read path. Owner search delegates case-insensitivity to column collation, and that mechanism is a known defect under PostgreSQL, whose schema stores the last name case-sensitively. The veterinarian reads are cached in the `vets` cache, which is created with statistics only — no size limit and no eviction.
+
+The filter's input arrives as a request parameter, so any caller chooses its value.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Fold case in the schema**, as owner search does — a case-insensitive column type or collation per vendor. Rejected: this is the mechanism behind the PostgreSQL owner-search defect, and it needs three separate vendor expressions.
+2. **Filter in memory** over the cached full collection. Rejected: it moves paging and the page totals out of the database and into the controller.
+3. **Filter in the database, case folded in the query, result cached** under `vets`. Rejected on the caching half: the cache key would carry a caller-supplied string into a cache that evicts nothing.
+4. **Filter in the database, case folded in the query, uncached** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+The specialty filter is a Spring Data derived query on `VetRepository` that folds case in the query itself. All three vendors therefore match alike, with no schema change.
+
+The filtered read methods carry no `@Cacheable` annotation. The unfiltered reads keep theirs.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Case-insensitive matching holds on every vendor, and the owner-search defect is not reproduced on a second surface.
+- Two searches in one codebase now fold case by different mechanisms. The owner search is the one out of step.
+- Folding case in the query cannot use the plain `specialties_name` index. The seeded specialty list is three rows, so the cost is not material at this size.
+- Every filtered request reaches the database. No caller can grow the unevictable `vets` cache by varying the parameter.
+- The cached unfiltered list and the uncached filtered list can disagree if veterinarian data changes out of band. No write path for veterinarians exists — see [Open Questions from the Survey](../system-design.md#open-questions-from-the-survey).
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-VET-003
+
+## References
+
+- [system-design.md#request-contracts](../system-design.md#request-contracts) — the published routes and the matching rule.
+- [ADR: Narrowing the Veterinarian Directory by Specialty Is In Scope](2026-08-23-non-goal-specialty-filter-narrows-vet-search.md) — the product decision this realizes.
+- [ADR: Feature-Package Organization Without a Service Layer](2026-07-31-feature-package-organization.md) — why the controller calls the repository directly.
